false},"title":"brsl/data_loader.py","time":{"start":1788373733255,"end":1788373733262}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"The loader works. 23,954 matches, 18,207 players. \n\nI notice the unified DataFrame still carries many extra columns from the concatenated frames (datetime, home_team_state, etc.) which is a bit messy. The spec wants clean unified columns. Let me refine the loader to drop the raw source-specific columns so the unified frame only has the canonical columns + the extended stat columns for br_football.\n\nAlso I notice \"Sport\" appears — that's a real team (Sport Club do Recife). Good.\n\nThe competition value_counts shows duplicate-ish competitions: \"Brasileirao Serie A\" (from brasileirao, 4180), \"Brasileirao Serie A (2003-2019)\" (from historico, 6886), and \"Serie A\"/\"Serie B\"/\"Serie C\" from br_football, plus \"Copa do Brasil\" from both copa and br_football, plus \"Copa Libertadores\".\n\nThis is fine — the query engine can normalize competition queries via the source field or aliases.\n\nLet me clean up the loader to drop extra raw columns. I'll modify `_finalize` to keep only the canonical columns plus the extended stat columns. Let me define the extra stat columns explicitly.\n\nLet me update _finalize to keep canonical + a defined set of extended columns. Also the historico `stadium` uses raw.get(\"Arena\") which may return a Series — that's fine in assign.\n\nLet me refine. I'll change the final columns list to include extended stats columns optionally present.\n\nActually the issue: when concatenating, all the raw columns from each frame get unioned, filling NaN. So the final df has tons of columns. I want to drop them. Let me update _finalize to select exactly the canonical columns and any of the EXTENDED_STAT_COLUMNS present.\n\nLet me edit the loader.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_063617eea001pzHdCRazhLixSV","sessionID":"ses_f9ca2d3d8ffe7GbwdSu72bCYg1","messageID":"ms