{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788373864235,"sessionID":"ses_f9ca2d3d8ffe7GbwdSu72bCYg1","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-9ab09365b708d28a","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/brsl/normalization.py","newString":"    if name is None:\n        return TeamName(\"\", \"\", None, None)\n    raw = str(name).strip()\n\n    # 0) strip a leading \"FC \" / \"SC \" / \"EC \" style prefix (FIFA exports).\n    m = re.match(r\"^([A-Z]{2})\\s+\", raw)\n    if m and m.group(1) in _CLUB_SUFFIX_TOKENS:\n        raw = raw[m.end():]\n","oldString":"    if name is None:\n        return TeamName(\"\", \"\", None, None)\n    raw = str(name).strip()\n"},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /workspace/brsl/normalization.py\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/brsl/normalization.py\n+++ /workspace/brsl/normalization.py\n@@ -88,8 +88,13 @@\n if name is None:\n     return TeamName(\"\", \"\", None, None)\n raw = str(name).strip()\n \n+# 0) strip a leading \"FC \" / \"SC \" / \"EC \" style prefix (FIFA exports).\n+m = re.match(r\"^([A-Z]{2})\\s+\", raw)\n+if m and m.group(1) in _CLUB_SUFFIX_TOKENS:\n+    raw = raw[m.end():]\n+\n state = None\n country = None\n \n # 1) trailing \" - STATE\" (2-letter Brazilian state abbreviation).\n","filediff":{"file":"/workspace/brsl/normalization.py","patch":"Index: /workspace/brsl/normalization.py\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/brsl/normalization.py\n+++ /workspace/brsl/normalization.py\n@@ -88,8 +88,13 @@\n if name is None:\n     return TeamName(\"\", \"\", None, None)\n raw = str(name).strip()\n \n+# 0) strip a leading \"FC \" / \"SC \" / \"EC \" style prefix (FIFA exports).\n+m = re.match(r\"^([A-Z]{2})\\s+\", raw)\n+if m and m.group(1) in _CLUB_SUFFIX_TOKENS:\n+    raw = raw[m.end():]\n+\n state = None\n country = None\n \n # 1) trailing \" - STATE\" (2-letter Brazilian state abbreviation).\n","additions":5,"deletions":0},"truncated":false},"title":"brsl/normalization.py","time":{"start":1788373864227,"end":1788373864232}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"One issue: \"FC Barcelona\" → key \"fc barcelona\" (FC not stripped because it's leading, my rule only strips trailing). But team_matches('Barcelona','FC Barcelona'): short \"barcelona\" (9 chars), long \"fc barcelona\" → \"barcelona\" in long.split() (['fc','barcelona']) → True. Good. But the display \"FC Barcelona\" has FC leading. For consistency in the graph, I'd prefer to strip leading FC too. But it's fine for matching.\n\nActually, to make the graph cleaner, let me also strip a leading FC/SC/EC/CF/AC/AA/SA prefix in normalize_team display. But the matches data doesn't have leading FC. The FIFA data does (\"FC Barcelona\", \"FC Barcelona\" etc.). Let me add leading-prefix stripping for the small set {FC, SC, EC, CF, AC, AA, SA} (2-letter all-caps suffixes used as prefixes). I'll strip a leading \"FC \"/\"SC \"/\"EC \"/\"CF \"/\"AC \"/\"AA \"/\"SA \" from the display.\n\nLet me add that to normalize_team before computing display/key. Actually the collapse already handles the key via contains-matching. For the display, I'll strip leading 2-letter all-caps prefix followed by space.\n\nLet me add it. In normalize_team, after computing `raw`, strip a leading prefix like \"FC \" \"SC \" etc.\n\nLet me edit.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_06363659c001TM0gTF3mMas6Ue","sessionID":"ses_f9ca2d3d8ffe7GbwdSu72bCYg1","messageID":"msg_063633d07001L4O4B1VHYIipha"}}
