{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788373975003,"sessionID":"ses_f9ca2d3d8ffe7GbwdSu72bCYg1","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-965f7765f78dd976","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /workspace && python3 - <<'PY' 2>&1\nfrom brsl import data_loader as dl\nm = dl.load_matches()\nfor src in m['source'].unique():\n    sub = m[m['source']==src]\n    print(f\"{src:16} seasons {int(sub['season'].min())}-{int(sub['season'].max())}  n={len(sub)}  comps={sorted(sub['competition'].unique())}\")\nprint(\"br_football date range:\", m[m['source']=='br_football']['date'].min(), m[m['source']=='br_football']['date'].max())\nPY"},"output":"brasileirao      seasons 2012-2022  n=4180  comps=['Brasileirao Serie A']\ncopa_do_brasil   seasons 2012-2021  n=1337  comps=['Copa do Brasil']\nlibertadores     seasons 2013-2022  n=1255  comps=['Copa Libertadores']\nbr_football      seasons 2014-2023  n=10296  comps=['Copa do Brasil', 'Serie A', 'Serie B', 'Serie C']\nhistorico        seasons 2003-2019  n=6886  comps=['Brasileirao Serie A (2003-2019)']\nbr_football date range: 2014-05-21 01:45:00 2023-12-07 00:30:00\n","metadata":{"output":"brasileirao      seasons 2012-2022  n=4180  comps=['Brasileirao Serie A']\ncopa_do_brasil   seasons 2012-2021  n=1337  comps=['Copa do Brasil']\nlibertadores     seasons 2013-2022  n=1255  comps=['Copa Libertadores']\nbr_football      seasons 2014-2023  n=10296  comps=['Copa do Brasil', 'Serie A', 'Serie B', 'Serie C']\nhistorico        seasons 2003-2019  n=6886  comps=['Brasileirao Serie A (2003-2019)']\nbr_football date range: 2014-05-21 01:45:00 2023-12-07 00:30:00\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"cd /workspace && python3 - <<'PY' 2>&1\nfrom brsl import data_loader as dl\nm = dl.load_matches()\nfor src in m['source'].unique():\n    sub = m[m['source']==src]\n    print(f\"{src:16} seasons {int(sub['season'].min())}-{int(sub['season'].max())}  n={len(sub)}  comps={sorted(sub['competition'].unique())}\")\nprint(\"br_football date range:\", m[m['source']=='br_football']['date'].min(), m[m['source']=='br_football']['date'].max())\nPY","time":{"start":1788373974920,"end":1788373974999}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Now the query_engine. This is the main logic with all the categories:\n1. Match queries: by team, date range, competition, season; head-to-head between two teams.\n2. Team queries: match history, win/loss/draw, goals, home/away record, performance by competition.\n3. Player queries: by name, nationality, club, ratings.\n4. Competition queries: standings by season (3 pts win, 1 draw), top scorers (can't infer individual scorers but can infer team goals), relegated.\n5. Statistical analysis: avg goals per match, biggest wins, home vs away, team performance trends.\n\nPlus head-to-head comparison and derbies.\n\nLet me design the query engine with functions returning dicts/lists (JSON-serializable) so the MCP server can return them.\n\nI'll implement a `QueryEngine` class wrapping `KnowledgeGraph`. Methods:\n- search_matches(team=None, opponent=None, competition=None, season=None, date_from=None, date_to=None, limit=...) -> list of match dicts\n- head_to_head(team_a, team_b) -> summary dict\n- team_stats(team, season=None, competition=None, home_away=None) -> dict\n- team_record_by_competition(team) -> dict\n- search_players(name=None, nationality=None, club=None, position=None, min_overall=None, order_by='overall', limit=...) -> list\n- top_brazilian_players(limit)\n- players_at_brazilian_clubs()\n- standings(competition, season) -> list sorted by points\n- biggest_wins(competition=None, limit) -> list\n- average_goals(competition=None, season=None) -> dict\n- home_vs_away(competition=None, season=None) -> dict\n- derbies(season=None) -> list\n- biggest_victories(competition=None, limit) -> same as biggest_wins\n\nLet me think about competition normalization. The matches df has competition labels: \"Brasileirao Serie A\", \"Brasileirao Serie A (2003-2019)\", \"Serie A\", \"Serie B\", \"Serie C\", \"Copa do Brasil\", \"Copa Libertadores\".\n\nFor a query \"brasileirao\" or \"serie a\" 2023, I should include \"Brasileirao Serie A\" + \"Serie A\" (the br_football ones) but for standings, \"Serie A\" from br_football and \"Brasileirao Serie A\" both represent Serie A matches. But they overlap in seasons? br_football has 2023 only (date range 2023-09-24 ... let me check). Actually br_football date range. Let me check the date range of br_football.\n\nLet me check the date ranges and which competitions overlap.\n\nActually for the standings query, the cleanest is to compute standings from a specific competition label set. For \"Brasileirao Serie A 2019\" I should use \"Brasileirao Serie A (2003-2019)\" (historico covers 2003-2019) plus \"Brasileirao Serie A\" (covers 2012-2023 per the spec file, 4180 matches). Wait — both have 2019? The brasileirao file (4180) — what seasons does it cover? Let me check. The historico covers 2003-2019. The brasileirao (Brasileirao_Matches) likely covers 2012-2023. So 2012-2019 appears in BOTH. That would double-count.\n\nHmm. This is a data overlap issue. For standings, I must avoid double counting. Let me check the season ranges of each source.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_063653561001Qt2wrw2STxeQs2","sessionID":"ses_f9ca2d3d8ffe7GbwdSu72bCYg1","messageID":"msg_0636493cb001D2xrHm51nzr6pt"}}
