{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788374103432,"sessionID":"ses_f9ca2d3d8ffe7GbwdSu72bCYg1","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-93c6752c9d25f3ee","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/brsl/data_loader.py","newString":"COMPETITION_ALIASES = {\n    \"brasileirao\": [\"brasileirao\", \"brasileirão\", \"serie a\", \"série a\",\n                    \"campeonato brasileiro\"],\n    \"copa_do_brasil\": [\"copa do brasil\", \"copa do brazil\", \"brazilian cup\",\n                       \"copa-do-brasil\"],\n    \"libertadores\": [\"libertadores\", \"copa libertadores\",\n                     \"libertadores da america\"],\n}\n\n# Map every competition *label* found in the data to a logical competition\n# \"bucket\" so that the same competition coming from different files (e.g.\n# \"Brasileirao Serie A\" and \"Serie A\") can be de-duplicated.\nCOMPETITION_BUCKETS = {\n    \"Brasileirao Serie A\": \"brasileirao\",\n    \"Brasileirao Serie A (2003-2019)\": \"brasileirao\",\n    \"Serie A\": \"brasileirao\",\n    \"Serie B\": \"serie_b\",\n    \"Serie C\": \"serie_c\",\n    \"Copa do Brasil\": \"copa_do_brasil\",\n    \"Copa Libertadores\": \"libertadores\",\n}\n\n# When the same physical match appears in more than one file, prefer the most\n# authoritative dedicated source.  Lower index == higher preference.\nSOURCE_PREFERENCE = [\"copa_do_brasil\", \"brasileirao\", \"libertadores\",\n                     \"historico\", \"br_football\"]\n\n\ndef competition_bucket(label: str) -> str | None:\n    \"\"\"Return the logical competition bucket for a raw competition label.\"\"\"\n    if label is None:\n        return None\n    return COMPETITION_BUCKETS.get(str(label))","oldString":"COMPETITION_ALIASES = {\n    \"brasileirao\": [\"brasileirao\", \"brasileirão\", \"serie a\", \"série a\",\n                    \"campeonato brasileiro\"],\n    \"copa_do_brasil\": [\"copa do brasil\", \"copa do brazil\", \"brazilian cup\",\n                       \"copa-do-brasil\"],\n    \"libertadores\": [\"libertadores\", \"copa libertadores\",\n                     \"libertadores da america\"],\n}"},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /workspace/brsl/data_loader.py\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/brsl/data_loader.py\n+++ /workspace/brsl/data_loader.py\n@@ -58,9 +58,34 @@\n     \"libertadores\": [\"libertadores\", \"copa libertadores\",\n                      \"libertadores da america\"],\n }\n \n+# Map every competition *label* found in the data to a logical competition\n+# \"bucket\" so that the same competition coming from different files (e.g.\n+# \"Brasileirao Serie A\" and \"Serie A\") can be de-duplicated.\n+COMPETITION_BUCKETS = {\n+    \"Brasileirao Serie A\": \"brasileirao\",\n+    \"Brasileirao Serie A (2003-2019)\": \"brasileirao\",\n+    \"Serie A\": \"brasileirao\",\n+    \"Serie B\": \"serie_b\",\n+    \"Serie C\": \"serie_c\",\n+    \"Copa do Brasil\": \"copa_do_brasil\",\n+    \"Copa Libertadores\": \"libertadores\",\n+}\n \n+# When the same physical match appears in more than one file, prefer the most\n+# authoritative dedicated source.  Lower index == higher preference.\n+SOURCE_PREFERENCE = [\"copa_do_brasil\", \"brasileirao\", \"libertadores\",\n+                     \"historico\", \"br_football\"]\n+\n+\n+def competition_bucket(label: str) -> str | None:\n+    \"\"\"Return the logical competition bucket for a raw competition label.\"\"\"\n+    if label is None:\n+        return None\n+    return COMPETITION_BUCKETS.get(str(label))\n+\n+\n def _data_path(filename: str) -> str:\n     return os.path.join(DATA_DIR, filename)\n \n \n","filediff":{"file":"/workspace/brsl/data_loader.py","patch":"Index: /workspace/brsl/data_loader.py\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/brsl/data_loader.py\n+++ /workspace/brsl/data_loader.py\n@@ -58,9 +58,34 @@\n     \"libertadores\": [\"libertadores\", \"copa libertadores\",\n                      \"libertadores da america\"],\n }\n \n+# Map every competition *label* found in the data to a logical competition\n+# \"bucket\" so that the same competition coming from different files (e.g.\n+# \"Brasileirao Serie A\" and \"Serie A\") can be de-duplicated.\n+COMPETITION_BUCKETS = {\n+    \"Brasileirao Serie A\": \"brasileirao\",\n+    \"Brasileirao Serie A (2003-2019)\": \"brasileirao\",\n+    \"Serie A\": \"brasileirao\",\n+    \"Serie B\": \"serie_b\",\n+    \"Serie C\": \"serie_c\",\n+    \"Copa do Brasil\": \"copa_do_brasil\",\n+    \"Copa Libertadores\": \"libertadores\",\n+}\n \n+# When the same physical match appears in more than one file, prefer the most\n+# authoritative dedicated source.  Lower index == higher preference.\n+SOURCE_PREFERENCE = [\"copa_do_brasil\", \"brasileirao\", \"libertadores\",\n+                     \"historico\", \"br_football\"]\n+\n+\n+def competition_bucket(label: str) -> str | None:\n+    \"\"\"Return the logical competition bucket for a raw competition label.\"\"\"\n+    if label is None:\n+        return None\n+    return COMPETITION_BUCKETS.get(str(label))\n+\n+\n def _data_path(filename: str) -> str:\n     return os.path.join(DATA_DIR, filename)\n \n \n","additions":25,"deletions":0},"truncated":false},"title":"brsl/data_loader.py","time":{"start":1788374103421,"end":1788374103427}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"So in 2019, the same Palmeiras vs Botafogo match appears in both `brasileirao` (date 2019-10-12 21:00:00) and `historico` (date 2019-10-12 00:00:00, time normalized to midnight). The date portion matches (2019-10-12) but time differs. So dedup by (date.date(), home_key, away_key, hg, ag) catches it → I'd keep brasileirao (preferred). Good.\n\nbr_football Serie A 2019 has 380 matches too — likely the same 380 as brasileirao 2019. Let me verify the Palmeiras-Botafogo 2019 in br_football. The earlier query for home=Palmeiras away=Botafogo only returned brasileirao and historico, not br_football. So br_football uses different team names (\"Sao Paulo\" without accents, \"Palmeiras\") — wait Palmeiras is the same. But the away_team_key in br_football for Botafogo... let me check. Actually the filter required home_team_key=='palmeiras' and away_team_key=='botafogo'. If br_football has it, it should appear. It didn't, meaning either br_football 2019 doesn't have that exact pairing or the team key differs. Let me not worry — the dedup by (date, home_key, away_key, hg, ag) will catch duplicates where keys align.\n\nThe key concern: br_football team names are accent-stripped (\"Sao Paulo\", \"Gremio\") so home_team_key for \"São Paulo\" → \"sao paulo\" and br_football \"Sao Paulo\" → \"sao paulo\". They align! Good. \"Grêmio\"→\"gremio\" and \"Gremio\"→\"gremio\" align. \"Botafogo\" same. So dedup should catch br_football/brasileirao duplicates for 2019 where dates and scores align.\n\nBut br_football dates include time (e.g., 2023-09-24 20:00:00) and brasileirao dates have time too. For the same match, the date portion should match. Let me dedup on date.date().\n\nHowever, there's a subtlety: br_football Serie A 2014-2022 overlaps with brasileirao 2014-2022. For season queries/team stats/head-to-head I want to dedup so the same match isn't counted twice.\n\nPlan: Build a deduplicated matches DataFrame in the knowledge graph (or data_loader) using a natural key:\nkey = (date.date(), competition_bucket, home_team_key, away_team_key, home_goal, away_goal)\nwith source preference order. Keep the first occurrence by preference. This yields a clean set for all aggregations.\n\ncompetition_bucket: map each competition label to a bucket:\n- \"Brasileirao Serie A\", \"Brasileirao Serie A (2003-2019)\", \"Serie A\" → \"brasileirao\"\n- \"Serie B\" → \"serie_b\"\n- \"Serie C\" → \"serie_c\"\n- \"Copa do Brasil\" → \"copa_do_brasil\"\n- \"Copa Libertadores\" → \"libertadores\"\n\nSource preference order (keep most authoritative first):\n1. copa_do_brasil (dedicated, accurate)\n2. brasileirao (dedicated)\n3. libertadores (dedicated)\n4. historico (2003-2019 Brasileirao)\n5. br_football (extended stats, catch-all)\n\nFor 2019 Brasileirao: both brasileirao and historico present, keys align on date+teams+score → keep brasileirao (preference 2 < 4). Good.\nFor 2019 br_football Serie A vs brasileirao: keep brasileirao (2 < 5). Good, but only if keys align. Let me trust they do.\n\nActually wait — is there a risk that the br_football match for the same game has a DIFFERENT date (e.g., timezone) such that date.date() differs by a day? Possibly. Then dedup misses and we double count a few. Acceptable for a demo; the vast majority align. Let me proceed.\n\nLet me also double check: does br_football \"Serie A\" 2019 contain the same 380 matches as brasileirao 2019? If dedup works, the deduped 2019 Brasileirao count should be 380 (from brasileirao), and br_football Serie A 2019 (also 380) would be dropped entirely as duplicates. Let me verify after implementing dedup.\n\nLet me implement the dedup in data_loader as a separate function `load_matches_deduplicated()` returning the deduped frame, and have the knowledge graph use it for aggregations. But the spec also wants raw \"search all files\" — I'll keep `load_matches()` raw (all 23,954) and add `load_matches_deduplicated()` for the graph's aggregation layer. The MCP search_matches can use raw (to show all), but team_stats/head_to_head/standings use deduped.\n\nHmm, but search_matches for \"Palmeiras 2019\" returning 760 (doubled) rows would look wrong. The spec's example \"Flamengo vs Fluminense ... (15 more matches in dataset)\" suggests they expect the natural count from the primary dataset. Let me use deduped for search_matches too, but tag each match with its source/competition so the user sees it came from the canonical file. Actually the example answer lists Brasileirão rounds, implying the primary brasileirao file. Let me use deduped matches for search_matches as well — cleaner.\n\nDecision: \n- `load_matches()` = raw union (all 23,954) — available for completeness/extended-stats.\n- `load_matches_deduplicated()` = the clean canonical set used by the graph & query engine for everything except extended-stat-only queries.\n- The KnowledgeGraph is built from the deduplicated set.\n\nLet me add `load_matches_deduplicated()` to data_loader and a `competition_bucket` helper.\n\nLet me implement. I'll add to data_loader:\n- COMPETITION_BUCKETS mapping\n- bucket_for_competition(label) -> bucket\n- load_matches_deduplicated() using source preference.\n\nLet me write this. I'll define:\nSOURCE_PREFERENCE = [\"copa_do_brasil\", \"brasileirao\", \"libertadores\", \"historico\", \"br_football\"]\nLower index = higher preference (keep).\n\nDedup: \n```\nm = load_matches()\nm = m.assign(_bucket=m['competition'].map(bucket_for_competition))\nm['_rank'] = m['source'].map(lambda s: SOURCE_PREFERENCE.index(s))\nm['_d'] = m['date'].dt.date\nm = m.sort_values('_rank')\nkey_cols = ['_d','_bucket','home_team_key','away_team_key','home_goal','away_goal']\ndeduped = m.drop_duplicates(subset=key_cols, keep='first')\nreturn deduped.drop(columns=['_rank','_d','_bucket'])\n```\nBut careful: NaN goals (100 rows) would group all NaN-goal matches with same date/bucket/teams into one — dropping duplicates would keep only one NaN match per (date,bucket,teams). That could wrongly collapse distinct matches. But there are only 100 NaN-goal rows and they're from br_football (draws? no — actually NaN goals). Let me handle: keep NaN goals distinct by also keying on index when goal is NaN. Simpler: only dedup rows where home_goal and away_goal are not NaN; leave NaN rows as-is (append them). Or: use `keep=False`? Let me just dedup on the key but for NaN goals, treat them as unique by substituting a unique value. I'll do: for the key, use home_goal.fillna(-1) but also include the row index for NaN ones. Simplest: dedup only among rows with non-null goals; concatenate the null-goal rows unchanged. There are only 100 null rows; fine.\n\nActually, let me just exclude NaN-goal rows from dedup and keep them all (they're a tiny fraction and won't materially affect stats). I'll do:\n```\nvalid = m[m['home_goal'].notna() & m['away_goal'].notna()]\nnulls = m[~m.index.isin(valid.index)]\ndeduped = valid.sort_values('_rank').drop_duplicates(key_cols, keep='first')\nresult = pd.concat([deduped, nulls], ignore_index=True)\n```\n\nLet me verify the dedup result count and 2019 Brasileirao count.\n\nLet me write the data_loader additions and test.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_063671ff7001lN9UcXSQgeEqEV","sessionID":"ses_f9ca2d3d8ffe7GbwdSu72bCYg1","messageID":"msg_06365ce34001pSzSvFxof4uV17"}}
