{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788374190169,"sessionID":"ses_f9ca2d3d8ffe7GbwdSu72bCYg1","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-91725d82faa900cf","state":{"status":"error","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/brsl/data_loader.py","newString":"@lru_cache(maxsize=1)\ndef load_matches_deduplicated() -> pd.DataFrame:\n    \"\"\"Return :func:`load_matches` with cross-file duplicate matches removed.\n\n    The same physical match frequently appears in more than one source file\n    (for example the 2019 Brasileirao is in both ``Brasileirao_Matches.csv`` and\n    ``novo_campeonato_brasileiro.csv``, and the BR-Football-Dataset overlaps\n    with all of them).  Duplicate detection keys on\n    ``(season, competition-bucket, home-team-key, away-team-key, home-goal,\n    away-goal)`` -- deliberately dropping the timestamp, which is recorded at\n    different precisions across files -- and keeps the most authoritative\n    source per :data:`SOURCE_PREFERENCE`.\n    \"\"\"\n    m = load_matches().copy()\n    m[\"_bucket\"] = m[\"competition\"].map(competition_bucket)\n    m[\"_rank\"] = m[\"source\"].map(lambda s: SOURCE_PREFERENCE.index(s))\n\n    has_goals = m[\"home_goal\"].notna() & m[\"away_goal\"].notna() & m[\"season\"].notna()\n    key_cols = [\"_bucket\", \"season\", \"home_team_key\", \"away_team_key\",\n                \"home_goal\", \"away_goal\"]\n    valid = m[has_goals].sort_values(\"_rank\")\n    deduped = valid.drop_duplicates(subset=key_cols, keep=\"first\")\n    nulls = m[~has_goals]\n    out = pd.concat([deduped, nulls], ignore_index=True)\n    return out.drop(columns=[\"_bucket\", \"_rank\"]).sort_values(\n        \"date\", kind=\"stable\").reset_index(drop=True)","oldString":"@lru_cache(maxsize=1)\ndef load_matches_deduplicated() -> pd.DataFrame:\n    \"\"\"Return :func:`load_matches` with cross-file duplicate matches removed.\n\n    The same physical match frequently appears in more than one source file\n    (for example the 2019 Brasileirao is in both ``Brasileirao_Matches.csv`` and\n    ``novo_campeonato_brasileiro.csv``, and the BR-Football-Dataset overlaps\n    with all of them).  Duplicate detection uses the tuple\n    ``(match-day, competition-bucket, home-team-key, away-team-key,\n    home-goal, away-goal)`` and keeps the most authoritative source per\n    :data:`SOURCE_PREFERENCE`.\n    \"\"\"\n    m = load_matches().copy()\n    m[\"_bucket\"] = m[\"competition\"].map(competition_bucket)\n    m[\"_d\"] = m[\"date\"].dt.date\n    m[\"_rank\"] = m[\"source\"].map(lambda s: SOURCE_PREFERENCE.index(s))\n\n    has_goals = m[\"home_goal\"].notna() & m[\"away_goal\"].notna()\n    key_cols = [\"_d\", \"_bucket\", \"home_team_key\", \"away_team_key\",\n                \"home_goal\", \"away_goal\"]\n    valid = m[has_goals].sort_values(\"_rank\")\n    deduped = valid.drop_duplicates(subset=key_cols, keep=\"first\")\n    nulls = m[~has_goals]\n    out = pd.concat([deduped, nulls], ignore_index=True)\n    return out.drop(columns=[\"_d\", \"_bucket\", \"_rank\"])"},"error":"Could not find oldString in the file. It must match exactly, including whitespace, indentation, and line endings.","time":{"start":1788374190141,"end":1788374190165}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Hmm, the dedup is working but there's a subtlety. In 2019 the deduped shows both \"Brasileirao Serie A\" (380, from brasileirao) and \"Brasileirao Serie A (2003-2019)\" (75, from historico, not overlapping with brasileirao dates?). And \"Serie A\" (219 from br_football). So the dedup didn't fully collapse the same competition because:\n\n1. historico 2019 (75 matches remaining) didn't dedup against brasileirao 2019 (380). Why only 75? Because historico 2019 had 380 but 305 matched brasileirao's 380 (same date+teams+score), leaving 75 that didn't match. Those 75 might be matches where the date or score differs between historico and brasileirao. Actually historically the historico file is 2003-2019 and the brasileirao file is 2012-2022, so 2012-2019 overlap. In 2019, 380 matches in historico and 380 in brasileirao; 305 deduped → 75 remain in historico because date/score didn't align exactly. \n\nHmm, this means the dedup isn't perfect — there are still duplicate matches (the 75 historico + some of the 380 brasileirao + 219 Serie A br_football might still overlap with each other).\n\nWait, the deduped 2019 \"Brasileirao Serie A\" = 380 (all from brasileirao), \"Brasileirao Serie A (2003-2019)\" = 75 (leftover historico), \"Serie A\" = 219 (br_football). So total 2019 Brasileirao-bucket deduped = 380+75+219 = 674 matches for one season of Serie A which should be ~380. So dedup is NOT collapsing across the bucket properly!\n\nWhy? Because my key uses `_bucket` but `drop_duplicates(subset=[\"_d\",\"_bucket\",\"home_team_key\",\"away_team_key\",\"home_goal\",\"away_goal\"])` — the bucket is the SAME for all three (all \"brasileirao\"). So duplicates with the same (date, bucket, home_key, away_key, hg, ag) across sources SHOULD collapse. But the 75 historico + 219 Serie A remain, meaning their (date, home_key, away_key, hg, ag) tuples don't match the brasileirao ones.\n\nThis is the date/time mismatch problem. historico dates are at midnight (00:00:00) while brasileirao dates have real times; but I used `_d = date.dt.date` so date portion. The Palmeiras-Botafogo example: brasileirao 2019-10-12 21:00 → date 2019-10-12; historico 2019-10-12 00:00 → date 2019-10-12. Same date. So those should collapse. And they did (380 - 75 = 305 collapsed). The 75 remaining are matches where the date in historico differs from brasileirao (maybe by a day, or different round assignment) OR the scores differ.\n\nAnd br_football Serie A 219 remaining (out of 380) — meaning 161 collapsed with brasileirao (same date+teams+score) but 219 didn't. The 219 likely have date differences (br_football might list different dates) or different team key mapping (e.g., br_football uses \"Sao Paulo\" → key \"sao paulo\", brasileirao uses \"São Paulo\" → \"sao paulo\", same). Hmm.\n\nThis imperfection means aggregations still double count somewhat (674 vs 380 for 2019 Serie A). That's a 1.77x overcount — bad for standings (would distort champion).\n\nI need a more robust dedup. The core issue: the same match across files may have different recorded dates (and the time portion). Let me use a looser key: (season, competition_bucket, home_team_key, away_team_key) WITHOUT date, but then different matches between the same two teams in the same season (home and away legs) would collide. To handle home/away legs, I could include the round. But round differs across files.\n\nAlternative robust dedup: key on (season, bucket, home_team_key, away_team_key, home_goal, away_goal) — i.e., drop the date, keep scores. The two legs (home and away) usually have different scores, and even if same teams home/away reversed, the home_team_key/away_team_key distinguishes the leg. So for a given season+bucket, (home_key, away_key, hg, ag) should uniquely identify a match leg in most cases (unless a team plays the same opponent twice with identical scoreline — rare). This would collapse the duplicate across files reliably.\n\nBut risk: if two DIFFERENT matches in the same season+bucket have identical (home,away,hg,ag) — e.g., two 0-0 draws between the same pair in the same season — they'd be wrongly collapsed. Rare but possible. For a demo benchmark this is acceptable and far better than 1.77x overcount.\n\nActually, let me think again. A cleaner approach: dedup by (season, bucket, home_team_key, away_team_key, hg, ag) but ALSO this collapses the home and away legs only if scores match exactly, which is uncommon. Good enough.\n\nBut wait, there's still the historico-vs-brasileirao date mismatch issue: if I drop date, the 75 historico leftovers that had different dates will now collapse with brasileirao (same season, bucket, teams, scores) → good. And br_football 219 will collapse too. Let me test with key = (season, bucket, home_key, away_key, hg, ag).\n\nActually even better: include the date but normalize to date-only AND handle the historico midnight. The leftover 75 in historico — let me check WHY they didn't match. Possibly the score differs (historico might have a different/walkover score) or the date is off by one day. Let me just drop date from the key to be safe, keeping season+bucket+teams+scores.\n\nLet me also reconsider: do I even want to merge historico with brasileirao? They're the same competition (Brasileirao Serie A) for overlapping years 2012-2019. Yes I want to merge to avoid double count. Dropping date from key handles it.\n\nLet me re-implement dedup key = (season, _bucket, home_team_key, away_team_key, home_goal, away_goal), keep first by source preference. Let me test the 2019 count.\n\nLet me update load_matches_deduplicated.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_06368667c001SLVZGidNuUZ8NT","sessionID":"ses_f9ca2d3d8ffe7GbwdSu72bCYg1","messageID":"msg_063677aff001L5igUaq5aD4Dof"}}
