{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788374307287,"sessionID":"ses_f9ca2d3d8ffe7GbwdSu72bCYg1","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-9b09fc1db0603206","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /workspace && python3 - <<'PY' 2>&1\nfrom brsl import data_loader as dl\nm = dl.load_matches()\ns19 = m[(m['source']=='brasileirao')&(m['season']==2019)]\ndef team_id(key,state): return key if state is None or pd.isna(state) else f\"{key}|{state}\"\nimport pandas as pd\ndata={}\nfor _,r in s19.iterrows():\n    for side in ('home','away'):\n        key=r[f'{side}_team_key']; st=r[f'{side}_state']; disp=r[f'{side}_team']\n        tid=team_id(key,st)\n        e=data.setdefault(tid,{'disp':disp,'state':st,'w':0,'d':0,'l':0,'gf':0,'ga':0,'pts':0})\n        gf=int(r['home_goal']) if side=='home' else int(r['away_goal'])\n        ga=int(r['away_goal']) if side=='home' else int(r['home_goal'])\n        if gf>ga: e['w']+=1; e['pts']+=3\n        elif gf<ga: e['l']+=1\n        else: e['d']+=1; e['pts']+=1\n        e['gf']+=gf; e['ga']+=ga\nrows=sorted(data.values(), key=lambda e:(-e['pts'],-e['w'],-(e['gf']-e['ga'])))\nprint(\"teams:\", len(rows))\nfor i,e in enumerate(rows[:5],1):\n    print(f\"{i}. {e['disp']}-{e['state']} {e['pts']}pts {e['w']}W{e['d']}D{e['l']}L GF{e['gf']} GA{e['ga']}\")\nPY"},"output":"teams: 20\n1. Flamengo-RJ 90pts 28W6D4L GF86 GA37\n2. Santos-SP 74pts 22W8D8L GF60 GA33\n3. Palmeiras-SP 74pts 21W11D6L GF61 GA32\n4. Gremio-RS 65pts 19W8D11L GF64 GA39\n5. Atletico-PR 64pts 18W10D10L GF51 GA32\n","metadata":{"output":"teams: 20\n1. Flamengo-RJ 90pts 28W6D4L GF86 GA37\n2. Santos-SP 74pts 22W8D8L GF60 GA33\n3. Palmeiras-SP 74pts 21W11D6L GF61 GA32\n4. Gremio-RS 65pts 19W8D11L GF64 GA39\n5. Atletico-PR 64pts 18W10D10L GF51 GA32\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"cd /workspace && python3 - <<'PY' 2>&1\nfrom brsl import data_loader as dl\nm = dl.load_matches()\ns19 = m[(m['source']=='brasileirao')&(m['season']==2019)]\ndef team_id(key,state): return key if state is None or pd.isna(state) else f\"{key}|{state}\"\nimport pandas as pd\ndata={}\nfor _,r in s19.iterrows():\n    for side in ('home','away'):\n        key=r[f'{side}_team_key']; st=r[f'{side}_state']; disp=r[f'{side}_team']\n        tid=team_id(key,st)\n        e=data.setdefault(tid,{'disp':disp,'state':st,'w':0,'d':0,'l':0,'gf':0,'ga':0,'pts':0})\n        gf=int(r['home_goal']) if side=='home' else int(r['away_goal'])\n        ga=int(r['away_goal']) if side=='home' else int(r['home_goal'])\n        if gf>ga: e['w']+=1; e['pts']+=3\n        elif gf<ga: e['l']+=1\n        else: e['d']+=1; e['pts']+=1\n        e['gf']+=gf; e['ga']+=ga\nrows=sorted(data.values(), key=lambda e:(-e['pts'],-e['w'],-(e['gf']-e['ga'])))\nprint(\"teams:\", len(rows))\nfor i,e in enumerate(rows[:5],1):\n    print(f\"{i}. {e['disp']}-{e['state']} {e['pts']}pts {e['w']}W{e['d']}D{e['l']}L GF{e['gf']} GA{e['ga']}\")\nPY","time":{"start":1788374307204,"end":1788374307282}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"So in the brasleirao source, \"Atletico\" appears with two states MG and PR but the display is just \"Atletico\" (accent stripped in this dataset). The home_team display is \"Atletico\" for both, distinguished only by home_state. So grouping by display \"Atletico\" merges them. I MUST use (home_team_key, home_state) or (display, state) as the identity.\n\nSo the team identity for standings should be (base_key, state). Let me make the standings/team-stats group by a composite `team_id = f\"{home_team_key}|{home_state}\"` and a display that includes state, e.g., \"Atlético-MG\". But the home_team display in brasleirao is \"Atletico\" (no accent, no state). I should construct a nicer display using the state. Actually, the normalized display stripped the state. For standings I can show \"Atlético-MG\" style. But the brasleirao display is \"Atletico\" (accent-stripped). I'll show \"Atletico-MG\" by appending state.\n\nHmm, but for the brasleirao file the original home_team was \"Atlético-MG\"? Let me check the raw. Actually the normalize_team stripped \"-MG\" and the accent → \"Atletico\". So the display lost the accent. For a nicer display I could keep accents but the brasleirao source original was \"Atlético-MG\" (with accent and state). Let me check the raw brasleirao file.\n\nActually for the standings output, I'll construct display as f\"{display}-{state}\" when state present, e.g. \"Atletico-MG\". Or better, since the original had accents, I could re-accent... too complex. I'll just use display + \"-\" + state.\n\nFor the 2019 standings with grouping by (key, state), Atletico-MG and Atletico-PR separate. Let me verify Flamengo is champion with 90 pts and Atletico-MG separate.\n\nLet me just build the standings using (home_team_key, home_state) grouping and check. Let me also decide: the team identity for the KnowledgeGraph teams dict should be (base_key, state) to avoid the Atletico collision. But br_football has no state → identity (base_key, None). So Palmeiras in br_football = (\"palmeiras\", None) vs brasleirao (\"palmeiras\",\"SP\"). Different identities → the graph would have 2 Palmeiras nodes. That's bad for \"what competitions has Palmeiras played in\".\n\nResolution: Use base_key as the PRIMARY identity for the graph (so Palmeiras is one node across files), BUT for standings/stats where state disambiguation matters, group by (base_key, state) using the source that has state.\n\nActually, the Atletico collision in the graph is a problem for team stats too. But for the spec's examples (\"Corinthians' home record\", \"Palmeiras\", \"Flamengo\") — none are Atletico, so the collision doesn't affect the headline examples. The Atletico ambiguity is an edge case. I'll handle it pragmatically:\n\n- Graph team nodes keyed by base_key (Palmeiras one node). For Atletico, the node represents all Atletico* teams combined — acceptable for \"what competitions has Atletico played in\" (shows MG and PR).\n- For standings & season team-stats, group by (base_key, state) when state available, else base_key. This gives correct Brasileirao standings (Atletico-MG vs Atletico-PR distinct) because the brasleirao source has state.\n\nLet me verify the 2019 standings with (key,state) grouping gives Flamengo champion 90 and the Atletico teams separate.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_0636a3a38001KpFBDIbs8FsLVI","sessionID":"ses_f9ca2d3d8ffe7GbwdSu72bCYg1","messageID":"msg_0636a089c001w2NI3b5aB4e6WW"}}
