{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788374934897,"sessionID":"ses_f9ca2d3d8ffe7GbwdSu72bCYg1","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call-bc5c17f1-3007-4fe6-b98e-5d4dcf8c1a45","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /workspace && python3 -m py_compile brsl/*.py tests/*.py && echo \"compile OK\" && python3 -c \"import brsl.server; s=brsl.server.build_server; print('entry import OK')\" && python3 -c \"from brsl.server import main; print('main callable:', callable(main))\""},"output":"compile OK\nentry import OK\nmain callable: True\n","metadata":{"output":"compile OK\nentry import OK\nmain callable: True\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"cd /workspace && python3 -m py_compile brsl/*.py tests/*.py && echo \"compile OK\" && python3 -c \"import brsl.server; s=brsl.server.build_server; print('entry import OK')\" && python3 -c \"from brsl.server import main; print('main callable:', callable(main))\"","time":{"start":1788374934629,"end":1788374934892}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"All queries well under the spec limits (<2s simple, <5s aggregate). The slowest are head_to_head (1.3s) and derbies (0.9s) due to iterrows+lambda over the full frame, but both under 2s. Good.\n\nNow let me address the \"code builds\" requirement. The package builds via pip install -e . which already succeeded. Let me verify a clean build / import and the console script works. Also there's no lint/typecheck config in the repo (stack.json tooling: none). The instructions say to run lint/typecheck if provided — none provided, so I'll skip. But let me make sure imports are clean and there are no obvious issues.\n\nLet me run a quick import check and the console script entry point (it would block on stdio, so I'll just check it imports).\n\nLet me also update README.md describing what was done (prompts.txt mentions updating README). The user's instruction was \"implement everything it asks for\" referring to TASK.md. TASK.md success criteria include functional requirements but not README update. The prompts.txt (ignored file) mentions README update as part of a sample prompt. I'll update README to describe the implementation since it's good practice and the README currently only has data source info. Let me update README.\n\nAlso, let me double check: the spec mentions \"MCP server connected to an LLM for query processing\" and \"knowledge graph interface\". I've built an MCP server with tools. Good. Neo4j wasn't mandated by TASK.md (only by the sample prompt in prompts.txt which is to be ignored). I used an in-memory graph. That satisfies \"knowledge graph interface\".\n\nLet me verify the console entry point imports without error and build a final clean check.\n\nLet me also make sure `python -m brsl.server` runs (will block, so just import check).\n\nLet me also run a syntax/compile check on all brsl files (python -m py_compile).\n\nLet me also double-check there are no leftover references to removed things. Let me run py_compile on the package and tests.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_06373acb2001MinX4K0MpgMtxI","sessionID":"ses_f9ca2d3d8ffe7GbwdSu72bCYg1","messageID":"msg_063738e1d001YtZxOrLPO18HCE"}}
